  "notes": "Same walk as tz-clock-test.json, run with --handle-mechanics 1 so pinned PinMAME's mechClock model (tz.c mech_add(0,&mechClock)) moves the clock and drives the eight clock optos. With the model on the ROM's power-up test report is empty, so the first service Enter shows the game information and the second opens the main menu; the sound-revision and PRESS ENTER FOR MAIN MENU steps of the model-off walk are dropped. The rest is unchanged: T.16 CLOCK TEST, then start and stop each of the four clock operations in turn, and every snapshot records the DMD, whose clock face and HOUR OPTOS boxes show the ROM's reading of the modelled optos.",
